          "text": "The pattern indexes as a primitive tetragonal phase. A consistent conventional cell is\n\n\\[\na \\simeq 5.575\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\qquad c \\simeq 6.219\\ \\text{\u00c5},\n\\]\n\nwith the low-angle reflections indexed as 001, 110, 111, 002, 200, 201, 112, etc. The missing 100 reflection and the observed sequence are consistent with **P4/nmm**. The structure is a ZrCuSiAs-related ordered Zr\u2013S/Zr\u2013Te stacking, with two formula units per cell.\n\nThe lattice parameters are well determined by the peak positions. The two free \\(z\\) coordinates are approximate powder-profile values and should be finalized by Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_Zr2TeS\n_audit_creation_method          'indexed and structure-matched from powder XRD'\n_chemical_name_common           'zirconium tellurium sulfide'\n_chemical_formula_sum           'Zr4 Te2 S2'\n_chemical_formula_structural    'Zr2TeS'\n_cell_formula_units_Z           2\n\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M  'P 4/n m m'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number     129\n\n_cell_length_a                  5.5753\n_cell_length_b                  5.5753\n_cell_length_c                  6.2190\n_cell_angle_alpha               90\n_cell_angle_beta                90\n_cell_angle_gamma               90\n_cell_volume                    193.27\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn   5.87\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength    1.5406\n\nloop_\n_symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz\n'x,y,z'\n'-x+1/2,-y+1/2,z'\n'-y+1/2,x,z'\n'y,-x+1/2,z'\n'-x,-y,-z'\n'x+1/2,y+1/2,-z'\n'y+1/2,-x,-z'\n'-y,x+1/2,-z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nS1    S     2  a   0.750000  0.250000  0.000000  1.0  0.8\nZr1   Zr    2  b   0.750000  0.250000  0.500000  1.0  0.6\nZr2   Zr    2  c   0.250000  0.250000  0.162000  1.0  0.6\nTe1   Te    2  c   0.250000  0.250000  0.676000  1.0  0.7\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| 2\u03b8 observed | hkl |\n|---:|:---|\n| 14.23\u00b0 | 001 |\n| 22.54\u00b0 | 110 |\n| 26.75\u00b0 | 111 |\n| 28.68\u00b0 | 002 |\n| 32.08\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 35.25\u00b0 | 201 |\n| 36.78\u00b0 | 112 |\n| 43.56\u00b0 | 202/003 |\n| 46.01\u00b0 | 220 |\n| 48.40\u00b0 | 221 |\n| 55.11\u00b0 | 222 |\n| 60.29\u00b0 | 312 |\n| 67.10\u00b0 | 400 |\n| 74.54\u00b0 | 404 |\n| 82.68\u00b0 | 424 |\n\nAn origin-reversed description, with \\(z_{\\rm Zr2}\\rightarrow1-z_{\\rm Zr2}\\) and \\(z_{\\rm Te}\\rightarrow1-z_{\\rm Te}\\), is crystallographically equivalent and is not a distinct alternative.",
